# Cloudflare Pages redirects. One rule per line: <from> <to> <status>
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# Purpose: keep every URL the WordPress site had indexed alive, so the
# rebuild does not shed search rankings or break inbound links.
#
# TWO ORDERING/MATCHING RULES THIS FILE DEPENDS ON — read before editing:
#
#  1. STATIC RULES FIRST, SPLATS AND PLACEHOLDERS LAST. Cloudflare resolves
#     static rules with a fast lookup, but any static rule sitting *below* a
#     splat or placeholder falls back to slow sequential matching. The build
#     log says so explicitly ("could be made more performant by bringing it
#     above any lines with splats or placeholders"). All dynamic rules are
#     therefore grouped at the bottom of this file.
#
#  2. MATCHING IS LITERAL — TRAILING SLASHES ARE NOT NORMALISED. `/blog-2`
#     and `/blog-2/` are different paths. WordPress served trailing-slash
#     URLs, so those are the forms actually indexed; every retired page below
#     carries both spellings. Omit one and the real legacy URL 404s.
#
# Splats (*) capture the rest of the path, including the empty string.
# Placeholders (:name) match exactly one non-empty path segment.

# ==========================================================================
