# --- Leadership bios: 10 individual pages consolidated onto one page ---
# :person, not *. A splat matches the empty string, so /who-we-are/leadership/*
# would match /who-we-are/leadership/ itself and redirect the real page to
# itself forever. A placeholder requires a non-empty segment. Both the bare and
# trailing-slash spellings are listed because matching is literal.
# They point at /who-we-are/, not the team page: that page is hidden pending
# discussion (docs/known-issues.md issue 22) and must not be reachable from a
# public link. Repoint them if it returns.
/who-we-are/leadership/:person            /who-we-are/  301
/who-we-are/leadership/:person/           /who-we-are/  301

